  "actor": "HARNESS",
  "what": "problem PD-1@v2 drafted",
  "phase": "DEFINE",
  "minute": 116.0,
  "event_seq": 271,
  "root_problem": "Billing dispute tickets roughly doubled from ~600/month to 1,180-1,260/month starting August 2026 (E-04), aligning with the 2026-08-01 deployment of billing-import rule BV-17, a high-consumption check comparing raw meter register values to 12-month m3 history with no unit scaling (E-12). Meter firmware v4.2 (rollout 2026-06) reports register readings in units of 0.1 m3 versus m3 for legacy v3.x firmware (E-13), so BV-17 treats v4.2 meters' normal readings as ~10x inflated; for the 1,240 disputed ESTIMATED-read bills this causes billing import to reject 1,184 valid AMI reads as REJECTED_HIGH_CONSUMPTION and substitute an estimate instead (E-11). This same unscaled-comparison defect is the best-supported candidate mechanism for the larger population of 1,785 disputed ACTUAL-read bills (E-01) as well, independent of any tariff change (ruled out, E-02) or response-time capacity shortfall (within SLA, E-03), though its reach into the ACTUAL-read population is not yet directly confirmed."
 },
